Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 06:39:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] updater: delete the installed update APK at startup

The in-app updater downloads update.apk into the external cache directory
and hands it to the system installer, but nothing removes the file after a
successful install (v0.21.0 only deletes it when the download fails), so
the last installer stays there until the next update overwrites it. Delete
it at startup once the version it holds is installed (or when it cannot be
read). Same change as Anikku Harmony patch 0011.

Rebased from the v0.20.4 series (0007): AppUpdateDownloadJob no longer
exists in v0.21.0 (the download moved into NewUpdateScreenModel), so the
helper lives in the new AppUpdateApkCleaner object and NewUpdateScreenModel
shares its file path.
